   108	// P1T-FIX1, review finding F01 (BLOCKING): a consumed DLPack manager may be the LAST owner of its memory (a bare capsule,
   109	// or a producer's temporary copy). Calling its deleter right after the launches let a producer on another stream reuse
   110	// the block before the legacy stream had read or written it (use-after-free, reproduced by addon_lifetime.py). Now
   111	// every consumed manager of a call that reached the launch stays alive until the legacy stream has passed that call:
   112	//   * RetainUntilComplete (constructed right before the launch, destroyed on scope exit, success OR exception after a
   113	//     partial launch) records one CUDA event on the operand device's legacy stream and moves every operand's manager
   114	//     into a module-level FIFO pending list together with that event;
