   130	// reusable events); CuPy's memory pool, which keeps freed blocks stream-ordered so a block is reused only in its own
   131	// stream's order (cupy/cuda/memory.pyx, 2017-); the DLPack consumer contract (dmlc/dlpack: the consumer calls the
   132	// deleter when it no longer needs the tensor); the CUDA rule that host callbacks must not call CUDA (CUDA Runtime API,
   133	// cudaLaunchHostFunc). Taken: event-fenced deferred release polled from the host, event reuse. Ours: applying it to
   134	// consumed DLPack managers on the consumer side, the GIL-held FIFO drain at every tc_signal entry point, the
   135	// count/bytes bound with a synchronize-and-drain fallback, and the leak-on-unfenceable rule.
   136	//
   137	// Construct it AFTER every validation and right BEFORE the first launch: the constructor may still throw (event
   138	// acquisition), and then nothing has been queued. Its destructor never throws.
