   682	// Phase 1: synchronize the legacy stream of the current device and of every device with pending entries (no deleter
   683	// runs, so iterating the live list is safe). Phase 2: pop entries in FIFO order and release each one whose event has
   684	// completed; leak (counted) an entry with no completion proof whose device could not be synchronized or whose event
   685	// query failed; stop at the first entry that is merely not ready on a device that DID synchronize: it was pushed after
   686	// phase 1 by a re-entrant call (a deleter that calls tc_signal) and is left pending. Every entry is popped before its
   687	// deleters run, so a re-entrant drain or bound drain pops each entry at most once. No allocation, never throws.
